  "assessment": [
    "Selection is read with a 256-KiB-plus-one rejection sentinel before JSON parsing, then must exactly match the immutable 16-file catalog. All identity/length/hash/license records are compared before parsing original contents.",
    "Actual 16 pinned originals total 141,571 bytes; largest is 47,058 bytes. Only the 2,403-byte adt-ui BUILD and 3,721-byte project-system-gradle-sync BUILD are lexed. Each wrong source content is length/hash rejected before discovery.",
    "Source reads stop at 4 MiB plus one; validated selected lengths have checked-add total at most 16 MiB. Lexer rejects more than 50,000 tokens and delimiter nesting beyond 32; parser rejects more than 64 top-level calls. Literal recursion is constrained by the prior lexical nesting bound.",
    "Borrowed token source slices avoid copying whole source per token. Separated literal views allocate pointer vectors across at most 32 nesting levels, while strings/containers are bounded by selected bytes and tokens. BTree containers preserve deterministic order with finite selected sizes.",
    "Protocol witnesses scan a fixed list of needles in hash-verified original sources, retaining exact matching excerpts; they do not recurse through a repository, follow class hierarchies, invoke Gradle/JVM, or discover arbitrary filesystem trees.",
    "Serialization uses checked-add plus fallible try_reserve in a 16-MiB BoundedWriter, completing encoding before output creation. Check mode reads bounded existing output and compares full bytes; create_new refuses replacement. File/collection lifetimes are ordinary Rust RAII, with no child processes, background tasks, external caches or native resources in this implementation.",
    "Actual normal locked xtask build/test receipts bind Fresh:false compiler artifacts to this current worktree. All 136 xtask tests and 22 membership regressions passed with zero failure/ignore/filter; repository Clippy and full formatting receipts passed.",
    "All 10 actual compiled CLI cases returned expected results: create/check plus 8 negative cases. The complete output is 53,129 bytes; create/check guarded stage durations were approximately 0.216/0.204 seconds in this environment. These owner timings include source-guard overhead and are observations, not benchmark guarantees."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "This is a fixed pinned-file CLI, not a general Starlark or arbitrary repository analyzer. The lexer computes indentation by rescanning the current line prefix, so adversarial long indentation combined with many tokens could be superlinear if the accepted catalog were broadened. Such altered contents are rejected before parsing in the reviewed command; this review does not certify generalized-input performance.",
    "No measured peak RSS, CPU profiling, IDE startup, UI responsiveness, large Android project, hardware-device or upstream compiled-runner performance evidence is claimed.",
    "A filesystem write failure can leave a newly created partial evidence file and returns an error; input originals and existing outputs are not replaced. Budget failure happens before opening the output. This review does not promise transactional/durable publication."
  ],
